    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 starting nine features a balanced offensive profile today, but **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leads the charge with an elite 73.66 projection. Facing Hughes, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup, making him our primary engine for Runs and AVG. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (68.63) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.18) are high-ceiling anchors; **Jacob Wilson** leverages a high 19% SP skill advantage against the vulnerable Me, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a must-start despite facing a tougher arm in Nola, as his floor is bolstered by consistently high base projections that remain resilient against tough pitching. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out our top-tier plays at 66.52, assuming he secures that leadoff spot, though his value is tethered to a 35% rain risk that bears watching.\n\nThe optimizer faced a difficult decision regarding the bench, ultimately excluding **Brayan Rocchio** (54.11) in favor of higher-floor starters. While **Brayan Rocchio** offers a solid 16% edge against Ober, the crowded middle infield and outfield landscape pushed him out. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** (53.28) was considered for his versatility, but his projected 8th-spot in the lineup suppressed his scoring ceiling compared to the primary lineup. We are also navigating caution with **Jackson Merrill**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Drake Baldwin**, all of whom are tied to potential rain disruptions. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slight negative platoon adjustment (-15%) against the lefty Bennett, his overall output remains too high to bench, though we will look for him to rely on his speed profile\u2014which remains a priority for the Waves\u2014to provide value even if the home run power is temporarily neutralized.",
